<id/04/0436/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Castor"@en ;
    skos:altLabel "beaver castor"@en, "castoreum"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_drugs_medicinal_botanicals/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "an animal substance possessing a disagreeable odour, obtained from the beaver, *Castor fiber*, and once much used as an antispasmodic in medicine. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 87]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated fields — source_taxon remove: Eurasian beaver; the rows are Canadian. | source_taxon add: North American beaver, source of the castoreum exported from Canada and Hudson's Bay. | bridge_1866 drop: The 1866 'Castor' concept is the castor-oil seed; this heading is castoreum."@en ;
